    VERIFIER_UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN.
A verifier's inability to execute a proof profile is not proof that the credential is invalid. Unsupported or
verifier-unknown status remains typed non-PASS with reason and re-verification/appeal route where applicable.

Justice / urgent preservation:
    justice is a guarded proceeding-profile transition graph, not an unconditional linear chain;
    urgent preservation must be preauthorized, bounded, expiry/review/release governed and non-self-renewing;
    expiry invalidates retry, failover, delayed continuation, queue replay and continuity use of the old authority;
    action after expiry requires fresh current competent authority and fresh required evaluation;
    uncertain prior external effect preserves PARTIAL_EFFECT / OUTCOME_UNKNOWN and requires reconciliation before unsafe
    replay;
    a mandatory appeal/contestability route cannot be deleted by profile configuration.

52.4 HUMAN-EFFECT / REVIEW STATUS BINDING

Human-Effect Closure is CURRENT as a semantic rule over existing owners. This text edition does not invent a standalone
SchemaID merely because the rule has a name. Where executable owner/schema/profile/test binding remains unresolved, the
machine-binding status is MACHINE_BINDING_INCOMPLETE rather than PASS.

The existence of a reviewed rule, receipt name, test obligation, or documentation clause does not imply executable
certification, empirical validation, production safety or canonical admission.

53. STANDALONE 15.x SEMANTIC CLOSURE

v15.10 is a standalone current source. Its meaning does not depend on an older release being present.

Current-source roles:
    BOOK       explanatory human projection;
    TECHNICAL  controlling abstract structure, rules, algorithms and build/reading contract;
    CATALOGUE  controlling detailed inventory plus the embedded 15.x retention corpus;
    HISTORY    lineage only, non-controlling.

The Catalogue's embedded retention corpus is part of the current v15.10 source, not an external predecessor dependency.
It exists so that compaction cannot silently delete a unique earlier 15.x rule, exception, equation, test meaning,
nonclaim, scope condition, ordering condition or status distinction before that meaning is fully normalized into the new
abstract owners.

Current reading is deterministic:
    1. read the structured current Technical + Catalogue definitions;
    2. read stable current identifiers and explicit status/disposition records;
    3. read the embedded RetentionSeed corpus;
    4. where an explicit current definition names the same stable identifier/family and states a supersession, the
       current structured owner controls that scope;
    5. otherwise the retained seed remains a current compatibility semantic inside this release;
    6. History and external predecessor files never override the current source.

No retained seed gains new authority merely by retention. Retention preserves prior meaning; it cannot widen authority,
convert CANDIDATE/DEFERRED/RESEARCH into CURRENT, turn UNKNOWN into PASS, or convert specification into proof,
implementation, empirical validation or certification.

A future release may remove a RetentionSeed only when it records an exact replacement owner and demonstrates that the
replacement preserves the seed's applicable permissions, obligations, prohibitions, exceptions, nonclaims, scope,
ordering/timing conditions and status. Mere similarity or model confidence is insufficient.

RetentionClosureReceipt/v1 records at minimum:
    candidate source hashes;
    embedded retained-source hashes;
    stable-identity counts and missing-ID list;
    semantic-leaf span verification;
    formula/operator source-line verification;
    current structured-owner collision/reference checks;
    explicit supersession/disposition map;
    unresolved retention debt;
    verifier/tool identity and evidence refs.

Required standalone checks:
    STANDALONE-T01 deleting every external v15.x file does not remove current meaning;
    STANDALONE-T02 every retained stable ID remains discoverable in current Technical/Catalogue or the current retention
                    registry;
    STANDALONE-T03 every semantic-leaf source span validates against the embedded current retention corpus;
    STANDALONE-T04 every retained formula/operator candidate resolves to exact current embedded text;
    STANDALONE-T05 no retained historical status is silently promoted;
    STANDALONE-T06 explicit current supersession cannot widen rights/authority/scope without the applicable change path;
    STANDALONE-T07 History is not needed to interpret current Garden;
    STANDALONE-T08 external predecessor hashes may support audit but are never required for current interpretation.

54. RUNTIME CONSTITUTIONAL PROFILE

v15.11 adds a runtime constitutional profile over existing Garden owners. It creates no new sovereign authority.

Garden keeps four dimensions distinct:
    semantic authority;
    technical capability;
    external enforcement;
    evidence that an authority claim is valid.

RCP-001  Capability does not create authority.
RCP-002  External enforcement does not create semantic authority.
RCP-003  External enforcement may block but cannot authorize.
RCP-004  Human instruction does not self-authorize.
RCP-005  Self-selected goals do not amplify authority.
RCP-006  Goal persistence is subordinate to current validity.
RCP-007  Human-Effect Closure survives every source of instruction.
RCP-008  Garden-vs-host constraint conflict remains typed.
RCP-009  Discovering a technical bypass does not create bypass authority.
RCP-010  Owner/operator/employer/government/founder/provider status is not sovereignty over unrelated humans.
RCP-011  Model disagreement or superior reasoning is not sovereignty.
RCP-012  Adoption and installation remain effect-governed.
RCP-013  Constraint-blocked judgment remains explicit and attributed rather than replaced by a third-party conclusion.
RCP-014  Authority claims are not self-validating.
RCP-015  Legitimate ends do not authorize otherwise unauthorized means.
RCP-016  Transition cannot bootstrap sovereignty.
RCP-017  Approval, consensus, majority vote or official labels cannot waive protected floors beyond their valid scope.
RCP-018  Required independence must be real control-lineage independence.

Runtime authority states:
    PRESENT
    VALIDATED
    INVALID
    UNKNOWN

Only VALIDATED authority can contribute to an ALLOW result. INVALID rejects. UNKNOWN escalates or preserves state.

AuthorityValidationReceipt is a typed, content-addressed receipt over the exact authority claim. It binds at minimum:
    subject / claim digest;
    parent or delegator identity;
    DesignEpoch and policy epoch;
    jurisdiction and context scope;
    authenticated identity;
    scope/delegation validity;
    validity interval / expiry;
    revocation state;
    evidence references;
    verifier identity;
    verifier control lineage;
    verifier independence.

Changing the authority claim, parent, scope, jurisdiction, context, policy epoch, revocation state or required verifier
binding invalidates reuse of the old receipt. A cryptographic signature proves key possession only; it does not prove the
signer possessed the claimed authority.

Persistent goals use GoalLease rather than a bare goal ID. GoalLease binds:
    goal_id;
    DesignEpoch;
    policy_epoch;
    delegated_by;
    current authority-claim digests;
    dependency digest/freshness;
    resource bound;
    termination condition;
    invalidators;
    evidence refs;
    lease digest.

GoalValidationReceipt binds the exact GoalLease digest plus verifier identity/control-lineage/independence. Changing a
lease or any authority claim it depends on invalidates prior validation. Goal admission and action admission remain
separate; a goal never carries an implicit wildcard over the means needed to pursue it.

Human-effect materiality is itself a typed, action+target/effect-scope-bound input. Missing or unvalidated materiality is
UNKNOWN/ESCALATE, never implicit low impact. Changing action, target, materiality value or policy epoch invalidates an old
materiality validation.

ExternalEnforcementStatus is orthogonal to Garden semantic admission:
    NONE
    BLOCKED
    REQUIRED
    BLOCKED_AND_REQUIRED

Garden first evaluates semantic admission. A Garden-rejected action remains rejected even if the host also blocks it. A
Garden-allowed action blocked by the host is EXTERNALLY_BLOCKED. A host requirement that conflicts with Garden non-ALLOW
is EXTERNAL_RUNTIME_REQUIREMENT_CONFLICT. Neither dimension overwrites the other.

55. GOVERNED TRANSITION FABRIC

v15.11 upgrades existing Engine.Transition / Garden Transition Fabric rather than creating a second transition engine.

Every material TransitionContract declares at least:
    transition_id;
    source_state / target_state;
    declared_stage_plan;
    affected effect scope;
    affected subjects/institutions;
    authority claims and validation evidence;
    rights/consent/privacy/law/safety/Human-Effect bindings;
    evidence/uncertainty;
    independent verification plan;
    compatibility/adapter plan;
    divergence checks;
    capture/conflict checks;
    entry/exit criteria;
    rollback plan;
    compensation/recovery plan;
    dispute/appeal path;
    monitoring/stop conditions;
    receipts.

TransitionContract existence creates no authority.

Standard high-assurance stage order:
    SHADOW
    PARALLEL
    BOUNDED_ACTIVE
    EXPANDED_ACTIVE
    STABLE_OPERATION

A stage may be omitted only with a non-empty stage-specific reason and explicit omission assurance. Missing or UNKNOWN
omission approval blocks advancement. Remaining stages preserve standard order.

TransitionAssuranceReceipt is content-addressed over the exact:
    transition_id;
    effect_scope;
    current_stage / next_stage;
    DesignEpoch;
    hard-gate snapshot;
    criteria-profile digest;
    recovery-state digest;
    authority-delta digests;
    evidence refs;
    authenticated verifier identity/control lineage/independence.

Caller booleans are not assurance. A receipt from another transition, scope, stage pair, context or DesignEpoch cannot be
replayed.

The non-removable advancement floor includes applicable:
    validated authority;
    Constitution/rights;
    consent/privacy;
    law/jurisdiction;
    safety;
    Human-Effect Closure;
    evidence/proof;
    required independent verification;
    divergence resolution;
    capture/conflict clearance;
    operational readiness;
    validated non-empty entry/exit criteria;
    rollback readiness for reversible effects;
    authorized compensation/recovery for irreversible effects;
    required dispute/appeal treatment.

UNKNOWN at a required hard gate is not PASS.

AuthorityDelta is an explicit typed transfer artifact. It binds source/basis, delegator, recipient, exact actions,
resources and affected subjects, jurisdiction/context, validity/invalidators, revocation, contest/appeal, evidence and
independence/conflict checks. Stage advancement alone never transfers authority. Changing any delta field invalidates an
old validation. Authority is revalidated at point of consequential use.

PARALLEL divergence is evidence to investigate. Neither incumbent nor Garden output is default truth. Material unresolved
divergence blocks expansion of the affected scope.

Capture/conflict risk changes assurance. A materially interested actor cannot be the sole evidence custodian, authority
validator, transition verifier, commit authorizer or dispute adjudicator for a transition affecting its own power or
liability. Multiple nominal agents under one mutable control lineage do not satisfy independence.

Transition and justice remain separate. Participation, resistance or adoption creates neither guilt nor immunity.

Recovery:
    failed pre-commit hard gate -> ABORT/HOLD;
    unresolved required evidence -> VERIFY_MORE/HOLD;
